; The implementer's fixture: a word and the words after it, one object a
; line. The newline is named, so the list of words stops at the line's end
; and a line of one word is refused.
lines = *( line %x0A / %x0A ) [ line ]   ; @array
line  = first rest                       ; @object first rest
first = ( TX )
rest  = 1*word                           ; @array
word  = ( TX )
